; Each frame beside the next in, each parameter's value and its step to the next frame out. A frame is 13 cards: V
; (1 voiced, 0 not), P (the pitch period in samples), A (the excitation amplitude) and K10 down to K1 (each
; reflection coefficient times 1000). The host deals the frames twice over, the second time from the second frame
; on, a card from each in turn, so that each card of a frame comes beside the same card of the next frame; the
; frames end with a record whose V is -1. For each frame it sends V, then for P, A and each K the value and the step,
; (next - this) / 10 by SFT 01. When the next frame's V differs (or there is none) there is no glide: the step is 0,
; by SFT 04.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frame   INP   v        03-14: V, and the next frame's: a glide (SFT 01) or none (SFT 04)
  04                    INP   nv
  05                    CLA   s404
  06                    STO   sft
  07                    CLA   nv
  08                    SUB   v
  09                    TAC   put
  10                    SUB   00
  11                    TAC   same
  12                    JMP   put
  13            same    CLA   s401
  14                    STO   sft
  15            put     OUT   v        15-31: V, then each value and its step
  16                    CLA   n11
  17                    STO   i
  18            each    INP   x
  19                    INP   c
  20                    OUT   x
  21                    CLA   c
  22                    SUB   x
  23            sft     DATA  0        (SFT 01 or SFT 04)
  24                    STO   d
  25                    OUT   d
  26                    CLA   i
  27                    SUB   00
  28                    STO   i
  29                    TAC   frame
  30                    JMP   each
  40            v       DATA  0
  41            nv      DATA  0
  42            x       DATA  0
  43            c       DATA  0
  44            d       DATA  0
  45            i       DATA  0
  46            n11     DATA  11
  47            s401    SFT   01
  48            s404    SFT   04
